    "text": "NON AG, NATALE SANCTI OSWALDI REGIS ET MARTYRIS.\n\u00c6FTER \u00d0AN \u00d0E AUGUSTINUS TO ENGLA LANDE BECOM w\u00e6s sum \u00e6\u00f0ele cyning Oswold\nSe ferde on his iugo\u00f0e fram his freondum and magum to Scotlande on s\u00e6, and \u00fe\u00e6r sona wear\u00f0 gefullod,\nBetwux \u00feam wear\u00f0 ofslagen Eadwine his eam, Nor\u00f0hymbra cynincg, on Crist gelyfed, fram Brytta\nAnd se Ceadwalla sloh and to sceame tucode \u00fea Nor\u00f0hymbran leode \u00e6fter heora hlafordes fylle, o\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6t\nOswold him com to, and him cenlice wi\u00f0feaht mid lytlum werode, ac his geleafa hine getrymde, and\nOswold \u00fea ar\u00e6rde ane rode sona Gode to wur\u00f0mynte \u00e6r \u00fean \u00fee he to \u00f0am gewinne come, and clypode\nGod sylf wat geare \u00fe\u00e6t we winna\u00f0 rihtlice wi\u00f0 \u00feysne re\u00f0an cyning, to ahredenne ure leode.\nHi feollon \u00fea ealle mid Oswolde on gebedum, and sy\u00fe\u00fean on o\u00f0erne mergen eodon to \u00feam gefeohte,\nSeo ylce rod si\u00f0\u00f0an \u00fee Oswold \u00fe\u00e6r ar\u00e6rde on wur\u00f0mynte \u00fe\u00e6r stod, and wurdon fela geh\u00e6lde untrumra\nSum man feoll on ise \u00fe\u00e6t his earm tob\u00e6rst, and l\u00e6g \u00fea on bedde gebrocod for\u00f0earle, o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t man him\nSeo stow is gehaten heofonfeld on englisc, wi\u00f0 \u00feone langan weall \u00fee \u00fea Romaniscan worhtan, \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6r\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a, Oswold ongann embe Godes willan to smeagenne, sona swa he rices geweold, and wolde\nSende \u00f0a to Scotlande, \u00fe\u00e6r se geleafa w\u00e6s \u00f0a, and b\u00e6d \u00f0a heofodmenn \u00fe\u00e6t hi his benum geti\u00feodon,\nHi sendon \u00fea sona \u00feam ges\u00e6ligan cyninge sumne arwur\u00f0ne bisceop, Aidan gehaten.\nSe w\u00e6s m\u00e6res lifes man on munuclicre drohtnunge, and he ealle woruldcara awearp fram his heortan,\nSwa hw\u00e6t swa him becom of \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges gifum, o\u00f0\u00f0e ricra manna, \u00fe\u00e6t he hra\u00f0e d\u00e6lde \u00feearfum and\nHw\u00e6t \u00f0a, Oswold cyning his cymes f\u00e6gnode, and hine arwur\u00f0lice underfeng his folce to \u00f0earfe, \u00fe\u00e6t\nHit gelamp \u00fea swa \u00fe\u00e6t se geleaffulla cyning gerehte his witan on heora agenum gereorde \u00fe\u00e6s bisceopes\nSe biscop \u00fea ferde bodigende geond eall Nor\u00f0hymbra lande geleafan and fulluht, and \u00fea leode gebigde\nHe lufode forh\u00e6fednysse and halige r\u00e6dinge, and iunge men teah georne mid lare, swa \u00fe\u00e6t ealle his\nSeldon he wolde ridan, ac si\u00f0ode on his fotum, and munuclice leofode betwux \u00f0am l\u00e6wedum folce,\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 se cynincg Oswold swi\u00f0e \u00e6lmesgeorn, and eadmod on \u00feeawum, and on eallum \u00feingum\nHit gelamp on sumne s\u00e6l \u00fe\u00e6t hi s\u00e6ton \u00e6tg\u00e6dere, Oswold and Aidan on \u00feam halgan easterd\u00e6ge; \u00fea b\u00e6r\n\u00dea sende se cyning sona \u00feam \u00feearfum \u00feone sylfrenan disc mid sande mid ealle, and het toceorfan \u00feone\n\u00dea genam Aidanus se \u00e6\u00f0ela bisceop \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges swy\u00feran hand mid swi\u00f0licre blysse, and clypode mid\nOswoldes cynerice wear\u00f0 gerymed \u00fea swy\u00f0e, swa \u00fe\u00e6t feower \u00feeoda hine underfengon to hlaforde,\nHe fulworhte on Eferwic \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6nlice mynster \u00fee his m\u00e6g Eadwine \u00e6r begunnon h\u00e6fde, and he swanc\nHe wolde \u00e6fter uhtsange oftost hine gebiddan, and on cyrcan standan on syndrigum gebedum of\nOn \u00feam ylcan timan com eac sum bisceop fram Rome byrig, Birinus gehaten, to Westsexena kyninge,\nBirinus witodlice gewende fram Rome be \u00f0\u00e6s papan r\u00e6de, \u00fee \u00f0a on Rome w\u00e6s, and behet \u00fe\u00e6t he\n\u00dea becom he to Westseaxan \u00fee w\u00e6s \u00f0a gyt h\u00e6\u00feen, and gebigde \u00feone cynincg Kynegyls to Gode, and\nHit gelamp \u00fea swa \u00fe\u00e6t se geleaffulla Oswold, Nor\u00f0hymbra cyning w\u00e6s cumen to Cynegylse, and hine\n\u00dea geafon \u00fea cynegas, Cynegyls and Oswold, \u00feam halgan Birine him to bisceopstole \u00fea burh\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Oswold cyning his cynedom geheold hlisfullice for worulde and mid micclum geleafan, and\nHit gewear\u00f0 swa be \u00feam \u00fe\u00e6t him wann on Penda, Myrcena cyning, \u00fee \u00e6t his m\u00e6ges slege \u00e6r\nHi comon \u00fea to gefeohte to Maserfelda begen, and fengon tog\u00e6dere o\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r feollon \u00fea Cristenan,\n\u00dea geseah he genealecan his lifes geendunge, and geb\u00e6d for his folc \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6r feallende sweolt, and\n\u00dea het se h\u00e6\u00feena cynincg his heafod ofaslean and his swi\u00f0ran earm, and settan hi to myrcelse.\n\u00dea \u00e6fter Oswoldes slege, feng Oswig his bro\u00f0or to Nor\u00f0hymbra rice, and rad mid werode to \u00fe\u00e6r his\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 gefylled swa we her fores\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6t his swi\u00f0re hand wuna\u00f0 hal mid \u00feam fl\u00e6sce, butan \u00e6lcere\nSe earm wear\u00fe geled arwur\u00f0lice on scrine of seolfre asmi\u00feod, on sancte Petres mynstre binnan\nHis bro\u00f0or dohtor eft si\u00f0\u00f0an on Myrcan wear\u00f0 cwen, and geaxode his ban and gebrohte hi to\nAc \u00fea mynstermenn noldon for menniscum gedwylde \u00feone sanct underfon, ac man sloh an geteld ofer\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea God geswutelode \u00fe\u00e6t he halig sanct w\u00e6s, swa \u00fe\u00e6t heofonlic leoht ofer \u00fe\u00e6t geteld astreht\n\u00dea wurdon \u00fea mynstermen micclum afyrhte, and b\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6s on mergen \u00fe\u00e6t hi moston \u00feone sanct mid\n\u00dea \u00f0woh man \u00fea halgan ban and b\u00e6r into \u00fe\u00e6re cyrcan arwur\u00f0lice on scrine, and gelogodon hi upp;\n\u00de\u00e6t w\u00e6ter \u00fee man \u00fea ban mid a\u00fewoh binnan \u00fe\u00e6re cyrcan wear\u00f0 agoten swa on anre hyrnan, and seo\nMid \u00feam duste wurdon afligde deofla fram mannum, \u00fea \u00fee on wodnysse \u00e6r w\u00e6ron gedrehte.\nEac swilce \u00fe\u00e6r he feol on \u00feam gefeohte ofslagen men namon \u00f0a eor\u00f0an to adligum mannum, and\nSum wegfarende man ferde wi\u00f0 \u00feone feld, \u00fea wear\u00f0 his hors gesicclod, and sona \u00fe\u00e6r feol,\nMid \u00feam \u00fee hit swa wealweode geond \u00feone widgillan feld, \u00fea becom hit embe lang \u00fe\u00e6r se cynincg\nSe ridda \u00fea ferde for\u00f0 on his weg \u00feider he gemynt h\u00e6fde.\n\u00dea w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6r an m\u00e6den licgende on paralisyn lange gebrocod; He began \u00fea to gereccenne hu him on\nHeo wear\u00f0 \u00f0a on sl\u00e6pe and sona eft awoc ansund eallum limum fram \u00feam egeslican broce; band \u00fea\nEft si\u00f0\u00f0an ferde eac sum \u00e6rendf\u00e6st ridda be \u00f0\u00e6re ylcan stowe, and geband on anum cla\u00fee of \u00feam\n\u00dea gemette he gebeoras bli\u00f0e \u00e6t \u00feam huse; he aheng \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6t dust on \u00e6nne heahne post and s\u00e6t mid\nMan worhte \u00fea micel fyr to middes \u00f0am gebeorum, and \u00fea spearcan wundon wi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6s rofes swy\u00f0e, o\u00f0\n\u00de\u00e6t hus wear\u00fe \u00f0a forburnon buton \u00feam anum poste \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t halige dust on ahangen w\u00e6s.\nSe post ana \u00e6tstod ansund mid \u00feam duste, and hi swy\u00f0e wundrodon \u00fe\u00e6s halgan weres geearnunga \u00fe\u00e6t\nAnd manega menn si\u00f0\u00f0an gesohton \u00feone stede heora h\u00e6le feccende, and heora freonda gehwilcum.\n\u00dea asprang his hlisa geond \u00fea land wide, and eac swilce to Irlande and eac su\u00fe to Franclande, swa swa\nSe preost cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t an wer w\u00e6re on Irlande gel\u00e6red, se ne gymde his lare, and he lithwon hogode\n\u00dea clypode he \u00feone preost \u00fee hit cydde eft \u00feus, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 him to sona mid sarlicre stemne, Nu ic\nNu wolde ic gebetan gif ic abidan moste, and to Gode gecyrran and to godum \u00feeawum, and min lif\nNu is us ges\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t sum halig cyning is on eowrum earde, Oswold gehaten; nu gif \u00feu \u00e6nig \u00feincg h\u00e6fst\n\u00d0a s\u00e6de se preost him, Ic h\u00e6bbe of \u00feam stocce \u00fee his heafod on stod, and gif \u00feu gelyfan wylt, \u00feu\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea se m\u00e6ssepreost \u00fe\u00e6s mannes ofhreow, and scof on halig w\u00e6ter of \u00feam halgan treowe, sealde\nFor\u00fey ne sceall nan mann aw\u00e6gan \u00fe\u00e6t he sylfwylles beh\u00e6t \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan Gode, \u00feonne he adlig bi\u00f0,\nNu cw\u00e6\u00f0 se halga Beda \u00fee \u00f0as boc gedihte, \u00fe\u00e6t hit nan wundor nys, \u00fe\u00e6t se halga cynincg\nNu h\u00e6f\u00f0 he \u00feone wur\u00f0mynt on \u00fe\u00e6re ecan worulde, mid \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan Gode, for his godnysse.\nEft se halga Cu\u00f0berht, \u00fea \u00fea he git cnapa w\u00e6s, geseah hu Godes \u00e6nglas feredon Aidanes sawle, \u00fe\u00e6s\n\u00de\u00e6s halgan Oswoldes ban wurdon eft gebroht \u00e6fter manegum gearum to Myrcena lande into\nSy \u00fe\u00e6s wuldor \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan Gode, \u00f0e on ecnysse rixa\u00f0 a to worulde; AMEN.",
